# Target C — Section 172: exact sign localization for the long-hull-side correction

**Date:** 2026-09-12
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**
**Status:** proof-only research candidate; theorem-state authority unchanged.
**Dependencies:** audited-working §§151 and 160, plus the Type-II loaded-hull side theorem.

The five-currency identity leaves the correction

\[
\chi_D:=q+m-\operatorname{per}(F)
\]

uncontrolled in sign.  The exact component remainder from §160 fixes its meaning:

\[
\boxed{\chi_D=\sum_r d_r+G_D+k-\operatorname{per}(F)-2.}
\tag{172.1}
\]

Here `d_r=diam(P_r)`, `G_D=R_I+s_B+\sum_r(\delta_r+2-d_r)\ge0`, and
`k=d_H+s_Z`.  Consequently, on every Type-II subsequence,

\[
\boxed{
\frac{\chi_D}{D}
\ge
\frac{1}{D}\sum_r d_r+\frac{G_D}{D}+\frac{k}{D}-\pi-o(1).
}
\tag{172.2}
\]

The negative-`\chi_D` branch is therefore a low total harmonic-diameter/remainder
profile, not an independent hull-side phenomenon.  Since the exact outer-walk identity
is

\[
\frac{b-\operatorname{per}(F)}{D}
=\frac{u_B+\chi_D}{D}\ge0,
\tag{172.3}
\]

any subsequence with `\chi_D\le-\varepsilon D` has

\[
\boxed{u_B\ge\varepsilon D.}
\tag{172.4}
\]

This is the precise transfer from a long-side deficit to the occurrence-counted
outer-walk surplus.

## 172.1 Finite identity

The audited §160 definition is

\[
G_D=2+q+m-k-\sum_r d_r.
\tag{172.5}
\]

Rearranging gives

\[
q+m=\sum_r d_r+G_D+k-2.
\tag{172.6}
\]

Subtracting `\operatorname{per}(F)` proves (172.1).  No asymptotic limit or sign
assumption is used.  The outer-walk ledger `b=q+m+u_B` then gives

\[
b-\operatorname{per}(F)=u_B+\chi_D,
\]

which proves (172.3)--(172.4), because an outer contact walk joining consecutive hull
vertices is no shorter than the corresponding chordal hull side sum.

## 172.2 Same-carrier quantitative lower bound

Suppose one harmonic carrier has strict-rhombus area at least

\[
A_{4,r}^{\rm int}\ge(A-o(1))D^2
\]

and normalized cell diameter `d_r/D\to\lambda`.  The audited §160 internal-face
isoperimetric estimate gives

\[
\frac{G_D}{D}
\ge[\sqrt{\pi A}-\lambda]_+-o(1).
\tag{172.7}
\]

Thus, on that same-carrier subsequence,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf\frac{\chi_D}{D}
\ge
S+[\sqrt{\pi A}-\lambda]_++\kappa-\pi,
}
\tag{172.8}
\]

whenever `\sum_r d_r/D\ge S-o(1)` and `k/D\to\kappa`.  The carrier and remainder
terms must refer to the same subsequence; no independent optimization is made.

At the audited Section-130/118 common-cap endpoint, the proof-only profile is

\[
S_*=2.798596312209462\ldots,
\quad
A_*=0.4703752868004241\ldots,
\quad
\lambda_*=0.9762439137425688\ldots .
\]

The §160 bound contributes

\[
\sqrt{\pi A_*}-\lambda_*
=0.239374260456223\ldots,
\]

so (172.8) yields the conditional endpoint estimate

\[
\boxed{
\frac{\chi_D}{D}
\ge-0.103622080924108\ldots+\frac{k}{D}-o(1).
}
\tag{172.9}
\]

In particular, if the endpoint branch also has `k=o(D)`, the negative correction is
bounded below by `-0.103623D+o(D)`.  A more negative long-side correction is impossible
there; by (172.4), it would require a correspondingly linear outer-walk surplus.

## 172.3 Scope and surviving obstruction

- Equation (172.1) is an exact finite Type-II identity under the audited §160 and
  loaded-hull side hypotheses.
- Equation (172.8) is conditional on a same-carrier quadratic area profile and the
  corresponding §160 isoperimetric bound.
- Contact-isolated source points remain outside all core diameter/rigidity statements.
- No claim is made that `\chi_D\ge0`, that `u_B=o(D)`, or that the endpoint profile is
  globally attainable.

The result sharpens the live closure target: any attempt to evade the favorable
five-currency correction through long nonunit hull sides must pay in one of two visible
places—at most the quantified harmonic/remainder deficit, or a linear outer-walk
surplus. A source-preserving diameter decrease, exact unit triangle, or independent
upper bound on that surplus is still missing. C-II remains open.

**Classification:** proved candidate awaiting promotion; proof-only.
